{offset200}{ia1}{offset0}
{arial}from: {arialbld}Kurt Rorscham{arial}
Krack of Molta











The Jaffa Tribune's headline reads: "{arialbld}THE RETURN OF THE FOX{arial}".
The Desert Echo's front page covers Alex Kolman: "{arialbld}THE STRATEGIST BEHIND THE VICTORY{arial}". We learn about his passion for chess and horticulture. 

Listen up! In the{arialbld}Meharist Gazette{arial} you scored the second page, there's an enthusiastic report about how you escaped certain death in directing your operations by ditching your jeep for a camel's back. 

The article is very well illustrated, complete with a photo of the animal, it even includes its pedigree up to five generations. 
These Sons of a Camel also published my predictions for the Jaffa Camel Chase, in the Comics...

To crown our victory, the Sheikh Al-Khadin, much thinner from his detention, has ordered a three-day banquet. Only we won't be there! Old Alex Kolman has emphasized our obligation to give no respite to the Psycho trio which succeeded in slipping through our fingers...

It's one of my Schyzo-States-Submersibles, SSS Pilobolus, which tracked down these runaways, having sighted in its periscope a convoy flying Tekton colours, heading due north.

Obviously this course leads straight to the Eolian Islands, the Psycho hideaway in the Platonik Sea where the three little pigs planned their picnic in Jaffar.

If his majesty Alex Kolman had followed my plan of sending a task force into the waters around the Eolian Islands, so as to cut off any retreat from those Tekton dodos, we would now be in the company of good old Youssef, relaxing on his cushions sipping his fig wine to the sound of the buzuki.

The Eolian Islands harbor three bases: Vulcano, Stromboli and Sirakruz.
Each of these beaches is decked with bunkers, so it won't be a piece of cake, but we do have a few good cards up our sleeve, four cruisers undergoing a refit that Tankred didn't have a chance to scupper (see below for a look at these beauties).














{center}{device23}

















What do you think {name} of livening it up, 5000 Eolian Lucras per base conquered, fair?



{offset50}Commander of the Schyzo Force 

{arialbld}Kurt Rorscham{arial}



